<title>SWEDEN: Swedbank Q1 profit rises 9 pct.</title>
<headline>Swedbank Q1 profit rises 9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish bank Swedbank on Wednesday posted its results for the three months ending March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating profit			  1,315 vs  1,202</p>
<p> Net interest income		     2,405 vs  2,400</p>
<p> Credit losses				 300 vs    460</p>
<p> Earnings per share (SKR)		 3.36 vs   3.10</p>
<p> Commission income			   977 vs   742</p>
<p> Commission expenses			 185 vs   146</p>
<p> Net income from financial ops	   117 vs   479</p>
<p> Other operating income		    224 vs   176</p>
<p> Total income				3,732 vs 3,853</p>
<p> Depreciation &amp; writedowns		 237 vs   255</p>
<p> Total expenses			    2,117 vs 2,191</p>
<p> Profit before loan losses	     1,615 vs 1,662</p>
<p> Net income				    934 vs   863</p>
<p> Capital adequacy ratio (pct)	  12.4  vs   11.8</p>
<p> Adjusted equity/share (crowns)	75.44 vs  61.28</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
